-- הסכם קיבוצי מיום 31.1.2001 — הסכם שכר לעובדים בשירות מי מהמעסיקים
-- לתקופה שמיום 1.1.99 ועד ליום 31.12.2001: the public-sector wage agreement
-- of the 1999–2001 round, between the State, the Centre of Local
-- Government, the three large cities, the institutions of higher
-- education, Hadassah, Clalit and the Jewish Agency, and the New General
-- Histadrut. The one-time grant of 1,250 for 1999–2000 (§2); the wage
-- supplement of 3.6% from 1.1.01 for 1999–2001, on the salary counted for
-- the hour value — the "תוספת 2001" later agreements name (§3); the
-- supplements outside that base raised by 3.6% (§4); the grades whose
-- supplement is left out of the minimum-wage completion, and the personal
-- supplement that keeps their pay from falling on promotion (§5); the
-- negotiation over the final rate to 31.7.2001 and the bar on any other
-- (§6); the structure of employment and the pensioners' update mechanism
-- left to further talks (§§7–8); industrial peace, disputes, earlier
-- terms, the follow-up committee and the agreed arbitration institution
-- (§§9–13). Annexed: the summary of 30.1.01 on the joint committee for the
-- pensions' update; the Finance Minister's letter on the research funds'
-- and friends' associations' employees; the wages commissioner's letter on
-- compensating the budgetary pensioners for the erosion of 1997–1999 (3.2%),
-- with its table of scales and the principles of the bill; and the summary
-- of 31.1.2001 between the Finance Minister and the Histadrut's chair on
-- the supplement to the pensions of the old funds' salary-ratio members.
--
-- It covers no teaching employee: its "עובד" (§2.1.1) is one whose pay is
-- computed by the agreements of a scale the Histadrut represents, and the
-- teaching scale is represented by הסתדרות המורים and ארגון המורים (the
-- Collective Agreements Law, §§15–16, imported). The teachers' agreement
-- of the round is Histadrut HaMorim's of 18.12.01, held against this one in
-- l4/tests/2001-12-18_histadrut-hamorim_wage-agreement-1999-2001-tests.l4.
-- The framework of 12.1.2011 names this agreement's 3.6% "תוספת 2001" and
-- imports this file. It speaks to no pay item of l4/lib/vocabulary.l4 and
-- is in no root. The formulas the pension summary computes by (its annex,
-- formulas 1–5) are not in the corpus, and a rule that needs one takes its
-- result as a named input.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT collective_agreements_law

§ `הסכם קיבוצי — הסכם שכר לעובדים בשירות מי מהמעסיקים לתקופה 1.1.99–31.12.2001 (31.1.2001)`

DECLARE `2001 framework action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the 2001 framework grant`
    `pay a former employee the 2001 framework grant he demands`
    `show the 2001 framework supplement on its own payslip line`
    `discuss a claim that a supplement belongs in the 2001 framework base`
    `act to recognise the 2001 framework supplement as fixed for the pensions law`
    `negotiate the final rate of the 2001 framework supplement`
    `negotiate further on pay for 1999–2001 before 1.8.01`
    `go on with the talks on the structure of employment, for 2001`
    `examine changing the update mechanism of the budgetary pensions`
    `strike over a matter the 2001 framework settled`
    `decide disputes over the 2001 framework`
    `examine the claims for the research funds' and friends' associations' employees`
    `announce the State's position on the research funds' employees`
    `initiate the bill compensating the budgetary pensioners for the erosion`
    `confirm the commissioner's letter of 31.1.2001 in writing`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The registration stamp: registered on 15.5.2001, number 100/2001; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 "Between"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p12 The employers' short name, "on the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p13 "And"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p14 The New General Histadrut and who represents it; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p15 The Histadrut's short name, "on the other side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p16 A recital: the parties negotiated a wage agreement for 1.1.99–31.12.2001.
-- akn:preamble/p17 A recital: a wage supplement and a one-time grant for 1999, 2000 and 2001, and a negotiation over the supplement's final rate, as set out below.
-- akn:preamble/p18 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

-- ¶3: made and signed on 31 January 2001.
@ref akn:preamble/p3
`the 2001 framework agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2001

-- ¶5–¶11: the employers that sign ("המעסיקים"): the State; the local
-- authorities through the Centre of Local Government (save the three large
-- cities); the three large cities; the institutions of higher education;
-- Hadassah; Clalit; the Jewish Agency, for itself and the World Zionist
-- Organisation, the Jewish National Fund and Keren Hayesod.
@ref akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11
`the employers that signed the 2001 framework` MEANS
    LIST "מדינת ישראל", "הרשויות המקומיות (מרכז השלטון המקומי)", "שלוש הערים הגדולות", "המוסדות להשכלה גבוהה",
         "הסתדרות מדיצינית הדסה", "שירותי בריאות כללית", "הסוכנות היהודית לארץ ישראל"

-- The agreement's period, as its title and first recital give it.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the 2001 framework agreement's period` d IF
        d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1999)
    AND d `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2001)

§§ `1 מבוא`

-- ¶1: the preamble and the annexes are part of it. ¶2: its headings are
-- for convenience only and do not bear on its reading.
@ref akn:art_1/p1
`the 2001 framework agreement's preamble and annexes are part of it` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_1/p2
`the 2001 framework agreement's headings bear on its reading` MEANS FALSE

§§ `2 מענק חד פעמי`

-- 2.1.1: an employee of the employers whose pay is computed by the
-- collective agreements of a scale the Histadrut represents ("עובד"),
-- employed in 1.1.99–31.12.2000 or part of it, has a one-time grant of
-- 1,250 ("המענק החד פעמי"); ¶: paid with the salary of February 2001 and
-- no later than March 2001's.
@desc An employee, as far as the agreement of 31.1.2001 asks.
DECLARE `2001 framework employee` HAS
    `employed by an employer that signed the 2001 framework` IS A BOOLEAN
    `his pay is computed by the agreements of a scale the Histadrut represents, for 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months employed in 1999–2000, for the 2001 framework` IS A NUMBER
    `employed on 1.1.01 or later, for the 2001 framework` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2-1-1
GIVEN e IS A `2001 framework employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an employee under the 2001 framework` e IF
        e's `employed by an employer that signed the 2001 framework`
    AND e's `his pay is computed by the agreements of a scale the Histadrut represents, for 2001`

GIVEN e IS A `2001 framework employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owed the 2001 framework grant` e IF
        `an employee under the 2001 framework` e
    AND e's `months employed in 1999–2000, for the 2001 framework` GREATER THAN 0

`the 2001 framework grant in full` MEANS 1250

GIVEN m IS A DATE @desc the first day of the salary month
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 framework grant may be paid with the salary of` m IF
        m `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2001)
    AND m `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2001)

`paying the 2001 framework grant` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2001 framework grant`

-- The same, as the Collective Agreements Law asks it (§§15–16): the kinds
-- of employee the agreement includes are the Histadrut's scales'. It does
-- not reach an employee of another kind, whoever employs him — so a
-- teaching employee, whose scale another organisation represents, is
-- outside it, and §23 never weighs it against a teachers' agreement.
GIVEN e IS A `2001 framework employee`
GIVETH AN `employee a collective agreement may reach`
DECIDE `the 2001 framework employee, as the law asks` e IS
    `employee a collective agreement may reach` WITH
        `his employer is a party to the agreement`  IS e's `employed by an employer that signed the 2001 framework`
        `his employer is represented for it by an employers' organisation that is a party` IS e's `employed by an employer that signed the 2001 framework`
        `his employer was or became a member of an employers' organisation that is a party` IS e's `employed by an employer that signed the 2001 framework`
        `his employer was expressly left out of the agreement` IS FALSE
        `he is of a kind of employee the agreement includes` IS e's `his pay is computed by the agreements of a scale the Histadrut represents, for 2001`
        `he is in an occupation or post the agreement includes` IS TRUE

-- 2.1.2: notwithstanding 2.1.1, an employer other than the State owes the
-- grant to one entitled to it who was dismissed or resigned, not into a
-- pension, before the signing, "only if he turns to the employer with a
-- demand for it within 30 days of his turning to the employer". A demand is
-- always within 30 days of itself: as printed, the limit has nothing to
-- bound. Read so that the 30 days do something (convention
-- reading.every-word; finding F-framework-2001-a): the duty arises on his
-- demand, and the employer pays within 30 days of it — as the teachers'
-- agreement of the round, §4.1.2, prints the same clause.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2-1-2
GIVEN `employed by the State` IS A BOOLEAN, `left before the signing, not into a pension` IS A BOOLEAN, `demanded the grant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer owes the 2001 framework grant to one who left` `employed by the State` `left before the signing, not into a pension` `demanded the grant` IF
       `employed by the State`
    OR NOT `left before the signing, not into a pension`
    OR `demanded the grant`

`paying a former employee the grant he demands` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay a former employee the 2001 framework grant he demands`
    WITHIN 30

-- As printed, a demand on any day is "within 30 days" of that same day.
`the 30 days of 2.1.2 bound nothing, as printed` MEANS
    all (GIVEN `the day of his demand` YIELD (`the day of his demand` MINUS `the day of his demand`) AT MOST 30)
        (range 0 3650)

-- 2.2: the grant is for 1999 and 2000, spread evenly over their months,
-- and paid by the position and the share of those years employed.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-2
GIVEN `months employed in 1999–2000` IS A NUMBER, `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 framework grant owed` `months employed in 1999–2000` `position fraction` IS
    `the 2001 framework grant in full` TIMES `position fraction` TIMES (min 24 `months employed in 1999–2000`) DIVIDED BY 24

-- 2.3: a budgetary pensioner has it too, by his pension rate and the share
-- of the months of 1999 and 2000 he received a pension.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-3
GIVEN `pension rate` IS A NUMBER, `months on pension in 1999–2000` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 framework grant a pensioner is owed` `pension rate` `months on pension in 1999–2000` IS
    `the 2001 framework grant in full` TIMES `pension rate` TIMES (min 24 `months on pension in 1999–2000`) DIVIDED BY 24

-- 2.4: the grant does not change the salary base of the table on the eve
-- of the signing. 2.5: notwithstanding any agreement, it is not salary for
-- any purpose, not counted for severance or the hour value, and no
-- contribution is made on it to a study fund, a provident fund, an
-- accruing pension fund or managers' insurance. 2.7: nor counted for the
-- completion to the minimum wage (the Minimum Wage Law is outside the
-- corpus).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-4 akn:art_2__para_2-5 akn:art_2__para_2-7
DECLARE `what a 2001 framework payment might count for` IS ONE OF
    `the 2001 framework table's salary base`
    `severance pay, for the 2001 framework`
    `the hour value, for the 2001 framework`
    `overtime, standby, shifts and incentive pay, for the 2001 framework`
    `a study fund, for the 2001 framework`
    `a provident fund, an accruing pension fund or managers' insurance, for the 2001 framework`
    `pensions, for the 2001 framework`
    `the completion to the minimum wage, for the 2001 framework`

GIVEN p IS A `what a 2001 framework payment might count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 framework grant counts for` p IF FALSE

`why the Minimum Wage Law is not in the 2001 framework` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק שכר מינימום, התשמ\"ז-1987"

-- 2.6: the grant does not exhaust the Histadrut's claims to change the
-- supplement's rate for 1.1.99–31.12.01.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-6
`the 2001 framework grant exhausts the claims on the supplement's rate` MEANS FALSE

§§ `3 תוספת שכר`

-- 3.1: an employee employed on 1.1.01 or later has, from 1.1.01, a wage
-- supplement of 3.6% for 1999, 2000 and 2001, on the base of 3.3 ("תוספת
-- השכר"); ¶2: paid with the salary of February 2001 and no later than
-- March 2001's.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 framework supplement rate on` d IS
    IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001) THEN `the 2001 framework supplement rate` ELSE 0

`the 2001 framework supplement rate` MEANS 3.6%

GIVEN e IS A `2001 framework employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owed the 2001 framework supplement` e IF
        `an employee under the 2001 framework` e
    AND e's `employed on 1.1.01 or later, for the 2001 framework`

GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the base of 3.3` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 framework supplement` d `the base of 3.3` IS
    `the 2001 framework supplement rate on` d TIMES `the base of 3.3`

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1/p2
GIVEN m IS A DATE @desc the first day of the salary month
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 framework supplement is first paid with the salary of` m IF
        m `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2001)
    AND m `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2001)

-- 3.2: on its own line of the payslip.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2
`showing the 2001 framework supplement on its own line` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `show the 2001 framework supplement on its own payslip line`

-- 3.3: the base is the combined salary, the seniority supplement and every
-- cost-of-living increment paid up to the supplement's payment, and every
-- supplement in shekels or in percent counted for the hour value
-- ("תוספות"), save 3.3.1 those not paid monthly, weekly or daily; 3.3.2
-- those not updated by the cost-of-living agreements, having a mechanism
-- of their own; 3.3.3 the completion to the minimum wage; 3.3.4 the
-- one-time grant of §2 and expense refunds.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-2 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-3 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-4
DECLARE `kind of 2001 framework pay component` IS ONE OF
    `the combined salary, the seniority supplement or a cost-of-living increment, for 2001`
    `another supplement in shekels or in percent, for 2001`
    `the one-time grant or an expense refund, for 2001`
    `the completion to the minimum wage, of 2001`

@desc A pay component, as §§3–4 of the agreement of 31.1.2001 tell them apart.
DECLARE `2001 framework pay component` HAS
    `the 2001 component's kind` IS A `kind of 2001 framework pay component`
    `the 2001 component is paid monthly, weekly or daily` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the 2001 component is updated by the cost-of-living agreements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc false where it has a mechanism of its own
    `the 2001 component is counted for the hour value` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN c IS A `2001 framework pay component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `one of 3.3.1–3.3.4` c IF
       NOT c's `the 2001 component is paid monthly, weekly or daily`
    OR NOT c's `the 2001 component is updated by the cost-of-living agreements`
    OR c's `the 2001 component's kind` EQUALS `the completion to the minimum wage, of 2001`
    OR c's `the 2001 component's kind` EQUALS `the one-time grant or an expense refund, for 2001`

GIVEN c IS A `2001 framework pay component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the base of the 2001 framework supplement` c IF
        NOT `one of 3.3.1–3.3.4` c
    AND (   c's `the 2001 component's kind` EQUALS `the combined salary, the seniority supplement or a cost-of-living increment, for 2001`
         OR c's `the 2001 component is counted for the hour value`)

-- 3.4: a claim of the Histadrut that a supplement of 3.3.1–3.3.4 belongs
-- in the base is discussed between the wages commissioner and the chair of
-- the trade-union department.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4
`a claim on 3.3's exceptions` MEANS
    PARTY `the wages commissioner`
    MUST  `discuss a claim that a supplement belongs in the 2001 framework base`

-- 3.5: the supplement is salary for every purpose: the hour value,
-- overtime with standby, duty, shifts, call-outs and incentive pay,
-- severance under the Severance Pay Law, 1963, pensions, pension and study
-- fund contributions, and every contribution usual on the combined salary.
-- (The minimum-wage completion is §5's.)
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5
GIVEN p IS A `what a 2001 framework payment might count for`, `in a grade 5.2 lists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 framework supplement counts for` p `in a grade 5.2 lists` IF
    IF p EQUALS `the completion to the minimum wage, for the 2001 framework`
    THEN NOT `in a grade 5.2 lists`
    ELSE NOT (p EQUALS `the 2001 framework table's salary base`)

`why the Severance Pay Law is not in the 2001 framework` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק פיצויי פיטורים, התשכ\"ג-1963"

-- 3.6: the same rate for every employee in every grade.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-6
`the 2001 framework supplement is uniform in every grade` MEANS TRUE

-- 3.7: the State acts to have it recognised as a fixed supplement for the
-- State Service (Pensions) Law (outside the corpus).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-7
`recognising the 2001 framework supplement for pension` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `act to recognise the 2001 framework supplement as fixed for the pensions law`

`why the State Service (Pensions) Law is not in the 2001 framework` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק שירות המדינה (גמלאות) [נוסח משולב], התש\"ל-1970"

§§ `4 תוספות שאינן מובאות בחשבון לערך שעה`

-- The supplements not counted for the hour value, and not among
-- 3.3.1–3.3.4, grow by 3.6% from 1.1.2001. With 3.3 this raises every
-- supplement but the four exceptions by the same rate: those in the base
-- through the supplement, the others by themselves.
@ref akn:art_4
GIVEN c IS A `2001 framework pay component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§4 of 2001 raises the component` c IF
        c's `the 2001 component's kind` EQUALS `another supplement in shekels or in percent, for 2001`
    AND NOT c's `the 2001 component is counted for the hour value`
    AND NOT `one of 3.3.1–3.3.4` c

GIVEN c IS A `2001 framework pay component`, `amount on the eve` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the component as §4 of 2001 raises it` c `amount on the eve` d IS
    IF `§4 of 2001 raises the component` c AND d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001)
    THEN `amount on the eve` TIMES (1 PLUS `the 2001 framework supplement rate`)
    ELSE `amount on the eve`

§§ `5 שכר מינימום`

-- 5.1: the supplement of §3 is not counted for the completion to the
-- minimum wage, but only in the scales and grades 5.2 lists. 5.2 (its
-- table): administrative 12–18+, מקצ"ט 5–11+, unified 4–9+, academics
-- (מח"ר) 35–39+, lawyers and prosecutors ג'–ד', journalists 35–39+,
-- certified X-ray 4–9, engineers 35–39+, technicians and practical
-- engineers 35–39+, social workers ח'–יא', biochemists and
-- microbiologists ב'–ה'1, pharmacists ב'–מ'1, nurses 10–12,
-- physiotherapists, occupational therapists and paramedical 1–3. Whether
-- an employee's grade is in his scale's span is an input. 5.3: save for
-- that, the supplement in those grades is the same as in any other.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-1 akn:art_5__para_5-2/t1 akn:art_5__para_5-3
`the scales and grade spans of 5.2` MEANS
    LIST (LIST "מינהלי", "12 – 18+"),
         (LIST "מקצ\"ט", "5 - 11+"),
         (LIST "אחיד", "4 - 9 +"),
         (LIST "מח\"ר", "35 – 39+"),
         (LIST "משפטנים ופרקליטים", "ג' – ד'"),
         (LIST "עיתונאים", "35 – 39+"),
         (LIST "רנטגן מוסמך", "4 - 9"),
         (LIST "מהנדסים", "35 – 39+"),
         (LIST "טכנאים והנדסאים", "35 – 39+"),
         (LIST "עובדים סוציאליים", "ח' - יא'"),
         (LIST "ביוכימאים ומיקרוביולוגים", "ב' - ה'1"),
         (LIST "רוקחים", "ב' - מ'1"),
         (LIST "אחיות", "10 - 12"),
         (LIST "פיזיותרפיסטים, מרפאים בעיסוק ופארה – רפואיים", "1 - 3")

`the scales 5.2 lists` MEANS
    map `the first of the row, of 2001` `the scales and grade spans of 5.2`

GIVEN row IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the first of the row, of 2001` row IS
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN s FOLLOWED BY rest THEN s
    OTHERWISE ""

GIVEN row IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the second of the row, of 2001` row IS
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN s FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `the first of the row, of 2001` rest
    OTHERWISE ""

GIVEN `his scale` IS A STRING, `his grade is in his scale's span in 5.2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in a grade 5.2 lists` `his scale` `his grade is in his scale's span in 5.2` IF
        elem `his scale` `the scales 5.2 lists`
    AND `his grade is in his scale's span in 5.2`

-- 5.4: the pay of an employee in a grade of 5.2's span that is the base of
-- the hour value, as it was on the eve of his rise to the grade above the
-- span's top, does not fall by that rise. 5.5: one left with a negative
-- difference has a personal supplement of the difference, offset against
-- every increase of the salary counted for the hour value save the
-- minimum-wage completion: 5.5.1 not counted for that completion; 5.5.2
-- offset from when he stops being owed the completion; 5.5.3 not offset
-- while the completion is paid again.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-4 akn:art_5__para_5-5
GIVEN `hour-value pay on the eve of the rise` IS A NUMBER, `hour-value pay after the rise` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 framework personal supplement` `hour-value pay on the eve of the rise` `hour-value pay after the rise` IS
    `not below zero` (`hour-value pay on the eve of the rise` MINUS `hour-value pay after the rise`)

@ref akn:art_5__para_5-5__subpara_5-5-1
`the 2001 framework personal supplement counts for the minimum-wage completion` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:art_5__para_5-5__subpara_5-5-2 akn:art_5__para_5-5__subpara_5-5-3
GIVEN `personal supplement` IS A NUMBER, `an increase of the hour-value pay` IS A NUMBER, `the minimum-wage completion is paid to him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2001 framework personal supplement after an increase` `personal supplement` `an increase of the hour-value pay` `the minimum-wage completion is paid to him` IS
    IF `the minimum-wage completion is paid to him`
    THEN `personal supplement`
    ELSE `not below zero` (`personal supplement` MINUS `an increase of the hour-value pay`)

§§ `6 קביעת שיעור סופי לתוספת השכר`

-- 6.1: from the signing to 31.7.2001 the parties negotiate the final rate
-- of the supplement for 1.1.99–31.12.01. 6.2: without derogating from 6.1,
-- no other negotiation is held until 31.7.01 on wage agreements or any
-- wage benefit for 1999, 2000 and 2001, nationally or at any other level,
-- for the employees it covers.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-1
`negotiating the final rate of 2001` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `negotiate the final rate of the 2001 framework supplement`

`the 2001 framework's negotiation ends on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 7 2001

@ref akn:art_6__para_6-2
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 framework bars other pay negotiations on` d IF
        d `is on or after` `the 2001 framework agreement was signed on`
    AND d `is on or before` `the 2001 framework's negotiation ends on`

`no other pay negotiation before 1.8.01` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `negotiate further on pay for 1999–2001 before 1.8.01`

§§ `7–8 מבנה העסקה וגמלאים`

-- §7: the talks on the structure of employment go on.
@ref akn:art_7/p1
`the talks on the structure of employment, for 2001` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `go on with the talks on the structure of employment, for 2001`

-- §8 ¶1: changing the update mechanism of the budgetary pensions under the
-- State Service (Pensions) Law to an agreed linkage is discussed in a joint
-- committee "as in the summary of 31.01.01". The summary annexed (its
-- first annex) is dated 30.1.01 and gives the committee its task from
-- 31.01.01; §8 is read as citing it (convention
-- instruments.cited-instrument-misdated; finding F-framework-2001-b). ¶2:
-- the section was signed following the wages commissioner's letter of
-- 31.01.01 to the chair of the trade-union department.
@ref akn:art_8/p1 akn:art_8/p2
`the joint committee on the pensions' update` MEANS
    PARTY `the joint committee`
    MUST  `examine changing the update mechanism of the budgetary pensions`

`the summary §8 of 2001 cites is dated, as printed` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2001
`the summary annexed to the 2001 framework is dated` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 1 2001

`the summary §8 of 2001 cites, as read` MEANS `the summary annexed to the 2001 framework is dated`

`§8 of 2001 dates the summary it cites a day after the annexed one` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the summary §8 of 2001 cites is dated, as printed`
    EQUALS DATE_SERIAL `the summary annexed to the 2001 framework is dated` PLUS 1

§§ `9–13 שקט תעשייתי, סכסוכים, הסכמים קודמים, ועדת מעקב ובוררות`

-- §9 ¶1: from the signing to 31.7.01 the Histadrut takes no strike, lockout
-- or other organised harm to work against any employer or unit, nationally
-- or locally, on the matters settled here. ¶2: the matters of §§7 and 8
-- are not matters settled here.
@ref akn:art_9/p1
`industrial peace under the 2001 framework` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `strike over a matter the 2001 framework settled`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2001 framework's industrial peace holds on` d IF
        d `is on or after` `the 2001 framework agreement was signed on`
    AND d `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 7 2001)

DECLARE `matter of the 2001 framework` IS ONE OF
    `the grant or the supplement, of 2001`
    `the structure of employment, of 2001`
    `the pensions' update mechanism, of 2001`

@ref akn:art_9/p2
GIVEN m IS A `matter of the 2001 framework`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a matter the 2001 framework settled` m IF
    m EQUALS `the grant or the supplement, of 2001`

-- §10: every collective dispute declared or announced, nationally or
-- locally, on the matters settled here is void with the signing.
@ref akn:art_10/p1
GIVEN `declared on` IS A DATE, m IS A `matter of the 2001 framework`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a labour dispute is void under the 2001 framework` `declared on` m IF
        `a matter the 2001 framework settled` m
    AND `declared on` `is on or before` `the 2001 framework agreement was signed on`

-- §11: the terms of earlier collective agreements, arrangements and
-- written undertakings stand for its period unless it amends or cancels
-- them, expressly or by implication.
@ref akn:art_11/p1
`earlier terms stand unless the 2001 framework changes them` MEANS TRUE

-- §12: a follow-up committee of the wages commissioner and the chair of
-- the trade-union department follows and helps carry it out and decides
-- disputes over it; ¶2: its decisions are final and bind the parties.
@ref akn:art_12/p1
`the 2001 framework's follow-up committee` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MAY   `decide disputes over the 2001 framework`

@ref akn:art_12/p2
`the 2001 framework follow-up committee's decisions are final` MEANS TRUE

-- §13: the agreement setting up the agreed arbitration institution in the
-- public services is extended as it stands, to the signing of the next
-- national wage agreement or for two years, whichever is earlier. The
-- arbitration agreement is outside the corpus.
@ref akn:art_13/p1
GIVEN `the next national wage agreement is signed on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the arbitration institution is extended to` `the next national wage agreement is signed on` IS
    CONSIDER `the next national wage agreement is signed on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `two years from the signing`
    WHEN JUST n THEN (IF n `is on or before` `two years from the signing` THEN n ELSE `two years from the signing`)
    WHERE
        `two years from the signing` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2003

`why the arbitration agreement is not in the 2001 framework` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "הסכם הקמת המוסד לבוררות מוסכמת בשירותים הציבוריים"

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 "In witness whereof the parties have signed"; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p2 The signatures; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/t1 The signature table: the State, the Histadrut and the other employers; no rule.

