-- ¶1: the erosion of the budgetary pensions of those who retired by
-- 31.12.99, against the active employees of the Histadrut's scales, in
-- October 1997–December 1999, 3.2%, is not in dispute.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1
`the erosion of the budgetary pensions, 1997–1999` MEANS 3.2%

-- ¶2: the government initiates a bill paying the pensioners compensation
-- for it; its principles (annexed) are for the civil service's budgetary
-- pensioners who retired by 31.12.99, in the scales of the annexed table,
-- paid from 1.1.2001 as a percentage of the pension.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1__para_2
`the erosion bill` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `initiate the bill compensating the budgetary pensioners for the erosion`

-- ¶3: that is a full and final exhaustion of the Histadrut's claims under
-- §10 of the framework agreement of 13.5.99 and its memorandum of the same
-- day, and of its claims on the erosion of the pensions of those who
-- retired by 31.12.99, for the time to 31.12.99.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1__para_3
