§§ `נספח: עקרונות הצעת החוק — תוספת לקצבה (פיצוי מיוחד)`

-- akn:att_5__hc_1/p1 The corpus's note naming the principles and their page in the scan; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1/p2 The bill's title: State Service (Pensions) (Supplement to the Pension – Special Compensation) (Temporary Provision), 2001; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1/p3 The heading "supplement to the pension"; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1/p2 The heading "non-application"; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1/p4 The heading "the schedule"; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1/p5 "(Section 1)": the schedule is §1's; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1/p6 A footnote: the Reshumot reference of the Pensions Law; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1/p7 The Treasury's address, partly illegible; no rule.

-- §1: one who retired from the civil service under the Pensions Law before
-- 1.1.2000, in a scale of the schedule, and is owed a pension, has from
-- January 2001 a monthly supplement of 3.2% of his pension. §2: not one who
-- retired as a policeman, a prison guard or an employee of the security
-- services. The schedule: the scales it lists.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_5__hc_1/t1
`the scales of the bill's schedule` MEANS
    LIST "הדירוג המנהלי", "דירוג המרפאים בעיסוק", "דירוג המה\"ר", "דירוג האחים והאחיות", "דירוג המהנדסים",
         "דירוג הביוכימאים והמיקרוביולוגים", "דירוג ההנדסאים והטכנאים", "דירוג טכנאי הרנטגן",
         "דירוג העיתונאים בשירות הציבורי", "דירוג הפארא-רפואיים (לרבות קלינאי תקשורת)", "דירוג המשפטנים",
         "דירוג העובדים הסוציאליים", "דירוג הפרקליטים", "דירוג מקצ\"ט", "דירוג הפסיכולוגים",
         "דירוג המפקחים הימיים", "דירוג הרוקחים", "דירוג הפיזיותרפיסטים"

GIVEN `retired on` IS A DATE, `his scale` IS A STRING, `retired as a policeman, prison guard or security employee` IS A BOOLEAN, `the pension month` IS A DATE, `his pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the bill's supplement to the pension` `retired on` `his scale` `retired as a policeman, prison guard or security employee` `the pension month` `his pension` IS
    IF      `retired on` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 1999)
        AND elem `his scale` `the scales of the bill's schedule`
        AND NOT `retired as a policeman, prison guard or security employee`
        AND `the pension month` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001)
    THEN `the erosion of the budgetary pensions, 1997–1999` TIMES `his pension`
    ELSE 0

§§ `נספח: סיכום דברים מיום 31/1/2001 — תוספת לפנסיה למבוטחים בשיטת יחסי השכר`

-- akn:att_6__hc_1/p1 The corpus's note naming the summary and its pages in the scan; no rule.
-- akn:att_6__hc_1/p2 The file number, partly illegible; no rule.
-- akn:att_6__hc_1/p3 The title, a summary of 31/1/2001; no rule.
-- akn:attachments/p21 The signatures; no rule.
-- akn:attachments/t2 The signatories: the Histadrut's chair and the Finance Minister; no rule.
-- akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_2__para_3__subpara_b/p3 The corpus's note on a page scanned out of order; no rule.
-- akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_2__para_3__subpara_b/p4 The corpus's note on a page scanned twice; no rule.

DECLARE `2001 pension summary party` IS ONE OF
    `the pension funds, under the 2001 summary`
    `the capital-market commissioner, under the 2001 summary`
    `the government and the Histadrut, under the 2001 summary`
    `the Histadrut, under the 2001 summary`
    `an employer that refused verification, under the 2001 summary`

DECLARE `2001 pension summary action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the advances on the pension supplement`
    `stop the advances on the pension supplement`
    `transfer the pensioners' group's part-time data`
    `verify the group's data and set its two rates`
    `pay the pension supplement by the general formula`
    `negotiate an agreed formula for the pension supplement`
    `transfer the interim group's part-time data`
    `transfer the active group's part-time data`
    `act to collect the active group's part-time data`
    `examine the collection of the part-time data`
    `let the commissioner verify its employees' data`
    `decide on the employees of the employers that refused verification`

-- The formulas of the summary's annex (1, the advance; 2, the mean of the
-- differences; 3, the general formula; 4, the part-time in the missing
-- period; 5, the rest) are not in the corpus: a rule that needs one takes
-- its result as an input.
`why the summary's formulas are not here` MEANS
    `the text is missing` "נוסחאות 1–5 בנספח לסיכום הדברים מיום 31/1/2001 (\"בנספח המצורף לסיכום דברים זה\")"

`why the summaries of 1996 and 1997 are not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "סיכומי הדברים בין שר האוצר לבין יו\"ר ההסתדרות מיום 10/5/1996 ומיום 8/12/1997"

-- ¶4: the summaries of 10/5/1996 and 8/12/1997, on a supplement to the
-- pension of the insured in the funds under the salary-ratio system ("the
-- supplement"), are carried out as below. §1: everything below is subject
-- to their conditions: 1.1 only the insured in the salary-ratio funds who
-- retired from 20/3/1996 are entitled; 1.2 only from the pension for
-- January 1998 on; 1.3 the supplement never exceeds 650 a month, linked to
-- the consumer price index from the index for December 1997.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1/p4 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3
GIVEN `insured under the salary-ratio system` IS A BOOLEAN, `retired on` IS A DATE, `the pension month` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the salary-ratio pension supplement for` `insured under the salary-ratio system` `retired on` `the pension month` IF
        `insured under the salary-ratio system`
    AND `retired on` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 3 1996)
    AND `the pension month` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1998)

GIVEN `the index for the month` IS A NUMBER, `the index for December 1997` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary-ratio pension supplement's cap` `the index for the month` `the index for December 1997` IS
    650 TIMES `the index for the month` DIVIDED BY `the index for December 1997`

GIVEN `by the formula` IS A NUMBER, `the index for the month` IS A NUMBER, `the index for December 1997` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary-ratio pension supplement, capped` `by the formula` `the index for the month` `the index for December 1997` IS
    min `by the formula` (`the salary-ratio pension supplement's cap` `the index for the month` `the index for December 1997`)

-- §2: the insured of every fund are three groups: 2.1 the pensioners,
-- retired from 20/3/1996 to 31/12/2000; 2.2 the interim group, retired from
-- 1/1/2001 to 30/6/2001; 2.3 the actives, due to retire from 1/7/2001.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3
DECLARE `2001 summary group` IS ONE OF
    `the pensioners' group, of 2001`
    `the interim group, of 2001`
    `the active group, of 2001`

GIVEN `retires on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `2001 summary group`
DECIDE `the 2001 summary group of one who retires on` `retires on` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `retires on` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2000) THEN `the pensioners' group, of 2001`
        IF `retires on` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2001) THEN `the interim group, of 2001`
        OTHERWISE `the active group, of 2001`

-- §3(א): the pensioners' group has five monthly payments on account of the
-- supplement, for the pensions of February to June 2001 only, subject to
-- 5.3; (ב) computed by formula 1 (not in the corpus) — set for this alone
-- and no basis for another; ¶2: one the formula gives nothing or less is
-- paid nothing; ¶5: the coefficient 0.3775 is agreed for formula 1 alone.
-- (ג) after the five months the pensioners are paid only under §5 or §6;
-- the payments on account never go on past them.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_2__para_3__subpara_a akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_2__para_3__subpara_b akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_2__para_3__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_2__para_3__subpara_b/p5 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_2__para_3__subpara_c
GIVEN `the pension month` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a month of the advances on the pension supplement` `the pension month` IF
        `the pension month` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2001)
    AND `the pension month` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2001)

GIVEN `the pension month` IS A DATE, `formula 1 gives` IS A NUMBER @desc formula 1 of the summary's annex, not in the corpus
      `the supplement by the general formula has started` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the advance on the pension supplement` `the pension month` `formula 1 gives` `the supplement by the general formula has started` IS
    IF     `a month of the advances on the pension supplement` `the pension month`
       AND NOT `the supplement by the general formula has started`
    THEN `not below zero` `formula 1 gives`
    ELSE 0

`the coefficient agreed for formula 1` MEANS 0.3775

`paying the advances` MEANS
    PARTY `the pension funds, under the 2001 summary`
    MUST  `pay the advances on the pension supplement`

-- §4(א): by 1/6/2001 the funds pass the capital-market commissioner ("the
-- commissioner") the pensioners' group's part-time data. (ב): if the data of
-- 85% of the group or more is passed, she verifies it against the
-- employers' within a month and sets two rates: (1) the share of the group
-- with full data — full only if part-time data exists for every month of
-- membership; the insured of an employer that refused verification are not
-- counted and are taken as outside the group — ("the full-data rate"); and
-- (2) the share, among those with full data, whose data has an error ("the
-- error rate"): an error is an absolute mean of the differences between the
-- employer's file and the fund's records over the whole membership above
-- 1%, the mean by formula 2 (not in the corpus). ¶2: the rates are set on
-- the data passed, which cannot be updated after.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_4__subpara_a
`transferring the pensioners' data` MEANS
    PARTY `the pension funds, under the 2001 summary`
    MUST  `transfer the pensioners' group's part-time data`

`the pensioners' data is due by` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2001

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_4__subpara_b akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_4__subpara_b/p2
GIVEN `the share of the group whose data was passed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commissioner verifies the group's data` `the share of the group whose data was passed` IF
    `the share of the group whose data was passed` AT LEAST 85%

`verifying a group's data` MEANS
    PARTY `the capital-market commissioner, under the 2001 summary`
    MUST  `verify the group's data and set its two rates`

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_4__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_4__subpara_b__cls_1/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_4__subpara_b__cls_1/p3 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_4__subpara_b__cls_1/p4
GIVEN `with full data` IS A NUMBER, `the group` IS A NUMBER, `of employers that refused verification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-data rate` `with full data` `the group` `of employers that refused verification` IS
    `with full data` DIVIDED BY (`the group` MINUS `of employers that refused verification`)

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_4__subpara_b__cls_2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_4__subpara_b__cls_2/p2
GIVEN `the mean of the differences, by formula 2` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an error in the insured's data` `the mean of the differences, by formula 2` IF
    `the mean of the differences, by formula 2` `is above` (1%)

-- §5: if the full-data rate is at least 85% and the error rate is no more
-- than 5% ("the criteria"): 5.1 from the first pension date after the
-- finding, the supplement is paid to every insured of the pensioners' group
-- with full and reliable data, as far as he is entitled, by his own data
-- and formula 3 ("the general formula"; not in the corpus); 5.2 with the
-- first payment, the supplements owed from his retirement or 1/1/1998,
-- whichever is later, to then, less what was paid on account under §3,
-- with index-linkage differences; 5.3 any advances not yet paid stop when
-- the supplement starts; 5.4 until 1.5.2002 the funds may pass the data of
-- the pensioners whose full data was not passed; they have no supplement
-- until the actives' data is examined, and then by §15.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_5
GIVEN `the full-data rate` IS A NUMBER, `the error rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the group's data meets the criteria` `the full-data rate` `the error rate` IF
        `the full-data rate` AT LEAST 85%
    AND `the error rate` AT MOST 5%

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_5__subpara_5-1
`paying the supplement by the general formula` MEANS
    PARTY `the pension funds, under the 2001 summary`
    MUST  `pay the pension supplement by the general formula`

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_5__subpara_5-2
GIVEN `retired on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the pensioners' arrears run from` `retired on` IS
    IF `retired on` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1998) THEN `retired on` ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1998

GIVEN `the supplements owed, linked` IS A NUMBER, `the advances paid, linked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the pensioners' arrears` `the supplements owed, linked` `the advances paid, linked` IS
    `the supplements owed, linked` MINUS `the advances paid, linked`

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_5__subpara_5-3
`stopping the advances` MEANS
    PARTY `the pension funds, under the 2001 summary`
    MUST  `stop the advances on the pension supplement`

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_5__subpara_5-4
`late data may be passed until` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 2002

-- §6: if the pensioners' data fails a criterion, the summaries are not
-- carried out by part-time data, for all the insured or any part of them;
-- the government and the Histadrut negotiate for six months an agreed
-- formula for all of them, and this summary is no basis for it.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_3__para_6
`negotiating an agreed formula` MEANS
    PARTY `the government and the Histadrut, under the 2001 summary`
    MUST  `negotiate an agreed formula for the pension supplement`

`the months to negotiate the agreed formula` MEANS 6

-- §7: if the supplement was paid to the pensioners under §5, the funds
-- pass the interim group's data by 1/8/2001. §8 (¶2–¶3): if 85% or more is
-- passed, she verifies it within a month and sets its two rates, on the
-- data passed. §9: if it meets the criteria of §5 (85% and 5%): 9.1 the
-- supplement by the general formula from the first pension date after;
-- 9.2 the arrears from his retirement, with linkage; 9.3 late data until
-- 1/5/2002, its owners paid by §15 after the actives' data is examined.
-- §10: if it fails one, the interim group joins the actives and has no
-- supplement until their data is examined.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_4__para_7
`transferring the interim data` MEANS
    PARTY `the pension funds, under the 2001 summary`
    MUST  `transfer the interim group's part-time data`

`the interim data is due by` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2001

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_4__para_8 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_4__para_8/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_4__para_8/p3 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_4__para_9 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_4__para_9__subpara_9-1 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_4__para_9__subpara_9-2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_4__para_9__subpara_9-3 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_4__para_10
GIVEN `the pensioners were paid under §5` IS A BOOLEAN, `the interim data meets the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `2001 summary group`
DECIDE `the group the interim insured are paid with` `the pensioners were paid under §5` `the interim data meets the criteria` IS
    IF `the pensioners were paid under §5` AND `the interim data meets the criteria`
    THEN `the interim group, of 2001`
    ELSE `the active group, of 2001`

-- §11: if the supplement was paid to the pensioners, the funds pass the
-- actives' data by 1/5/2002. §12 (¶2): if 85% or more is passed, she
-- verifies it within four months and sets its two rates. §13: if it meets
-- the criteria: 13.1 each active who retired, with full and reliable data,
-- is paid by the general formula from the first pension date after; 13.2
-- with arrears from his retirement, linked; 13.3 the Histadrut acts to
-- have the actives' data collected in every fund from the signing, and the
-- commissioner may examine the collection and the data.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_11
`transferring the active data` MEANS
    PARTY `the pension funds, under the 2001 summary`
    MUST  `transfer the active group's part-time data`

`the active data is due by` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 2002

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_12 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_12/p2
GIVEN `the group` IS A `2001 summary group`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the months the commissioner has to verify` `the group` IS
    IF `the group` EQUALS `the active group, of 2001` THEN 4 ELSE 1

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_13 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_13__subpara_13-1 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_13__subpara_13-2
GIVEN `retired on` IS A DATE, `the group` IS A `2001 summary group`
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the arrears of the general formula run from` `retired on` `the group` IS
    IF `the group` EQUALS `the pensioners' group, of 2001`
    THEN `the pensioners' arrears run from` `retired on`
    ELSE `retired on`

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_13__subpara_13-3
`collecting the actives' data` MEANS
    PARTY `the Histadrut, under the 2001 summary`
    MUST  `act to collect the active group's part-time data`

`examining the collection` MEANS
    PARTY `the capital-market commissioner, under the 2001 summary`
    MAY   `examine the collection of the part-time data`

-- §14: if the actives' data fails a criterion: 14.1 the summaries are not
-- carried out for them by part-time data, and the government and the
-- Histadrut negotiate an agreed formula, this summary no basis for it;
-- 14.2 the supplement to the pensioners with full data goes on by the
-- general formula; 14.3 so does the interim group's, if begun; 14.4 every
-- other insured is paid by the agreed formula of 14.1.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_14 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_14__subpara_14-1 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_14__subpara_14-2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_14__subpara_14-3 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_5__para_14__subpara_14-4
DECLARE `2001 summary formula` IS ONE OF
    `the general formula, of 2001`
    `formula 4 for the missing part-time, of 2001`
    `formula 5 for the rest, of 2001`
    `the agreed formula still to be negotiated, of 2001`
    `no supplement yet, of 2001`

GIVEN `the actives' data meets the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid by the general formula already` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a pensioner, or an interim insured, with full data, whose supplement began under §5 or §9
GIVETH A `2001 summary formula`
DECIDE `the formula after the actives' data fails` `the actives' data meets the criteria` `paid by the general formula already` IS
    IF `the actives' data meets the criteria` OR `paid by the general formula already`
    THEN `the general formula, of 2001`
    ELSE `the agreed formula still to be negotiated, of 2001`

-- §15 (¶2): if the actives' data meets the criteria, the supplement of the
-- insured of all three groups without full data is computed as below, paid
-- when the actives with full data are paid. 15.1: one with full part-time
-- data for his last three years of membership is paid as if his data were
-- full, the missing data filled: 15.1.1 where the period without data is
-- up to 15% of his membership and no more than 42 months, his average
-- part-time in the period with data stands for the whole; 15.1.2 one
-- missing data of earlier periods has his part-time from joining to the
-- first day from which his data runs full and unbroken to the end ("the
-- start of the data's run") by formula 4 (not in the corpus); 15.1.3 one
-- whose data is missing for work in a factory that closed: 15.1.3.1 his
-- run starts on the first day from which it is full and unbroken but for
-- that factory; 15.1.3.2 his part-time to then, and in the factory, by
-- formula 4. 15.2: the rest, with no data and outside 15.1, by formula 5.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_6__para_15 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_6__para_15/p2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_6__para_15__subpara_15-1 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_6__para_15__subpara_15-1__cls_15-1-1 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_6__para_15__subpara_15-1__cls_15-1-2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_6__para_15__subpara_15-1__cls_15-1-3 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_6__para_15__subpara_15-1__cls_15-1-3__pnt_15-1-3-1 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_6__para_15__subpara_15-1__cls_15-1-3__pnt_15-1-3-2 akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_6__para_15__subpara_15-2
@desc One insured without full part-time data, as §15 of the summary tells them apart.
DECLARE `2001 summary insured without full data` HAS
    `full data for his last three years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of membership` IS A NUMBER
    `months without data` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN i IS A `2001 summary insured without full data`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `his average part-time stands for the whole` i IF
        i's `full data for his last three years`
    AND i's `months without data` AT MOST 42
    AND i's `months without data` AT MOST (15% TIMES i's `months of membership`)

GIVEN `the actives' data meets the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN, i IS A `2001 summary insured without full data`
GIVETH A `2001 summary formula`
DECIDE `how §15 computes his supplement` `the actives' data meets the criteria` i IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the actives' data meets the criteria` THEN `the agreed formula still to be negotiated, of 2001`
        IF `his average part-time stands for the whole` i THEN `the general formula, of 2001`
        IF i's `full data for his last three years` THEN `formula 4 for the missing part-time, of 2001`
        OTHERWISE `formula 5 for the rest, of 2001`

-- §16(א): an employer whose insured were not counted (4(ב)(1)) for refusing
-- verification may allow it until 1/5/2002; if it does, they join the
-- actives. (ב): within six months after 1.5.2002 the government's and the
-- Histadrut's representatives decide what is done for the employees and
-- pensioners of employers that had not allowed it by then, including
-- whether they are paid the supplement.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_6__para_16__subpara_a
`letting the commissioner verify late` MEANS
    PARTY `an employer that refused verification, under the 2001 summary`
    MAY   `let the commissioner verify its employees' data`

@ref akn:att_6__hc_1__hc_6__para_16__subpara_b
`deciding on the refusing employers' insured` MEANS
    PARTY `the government and the Histadrut, under the 2001 summary`
    MUST  `decide on the employees of the employers that refused verification`

`the decision on the refusing employers is due by` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2002

-- ¶5: nothing here takes from the funds' right to change their insured's
-- pension rights under the rules and arrangements known today, carried out
-- or not; a change that bears on the supplement of one not yet retired
-- when it is made applies to computing his supplement too.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1/p5
GIVEN `the change was made on` IS A DATE, `he retired on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a fund's change applies to his supplement` `the change was made on` `he retired on` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `he retired on` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the change was made on`

§§ `ממצאים`

-- F-framework-2001-a: 2.1.2's 30 days run from the demand they bound.
#ASSERT `the 30 days of 2.1.2 bound nothing, as printed`

-- F-framework-2001-b: §8 dates the annexed summary a day late.
#ASSERT `§8 of 2001 dates the summary it cites a day after the annexed one`

§§ `דוגמאות`

`a nurse of the State in 2001` MEANS `2001 framework employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the 2001 framework` IS TRUE
    `his pay is computed by the agreements of a scale the Histadrut represents, for 2001` IS TRUE
    `months employed in 1999–2000, for the 2001 framework` IS 24
    `employed on 1.1.01 or later, for the 2001 framework` IS TRUE
`a teacher of the State in 2001` MEANS `2001 framework employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the 2001 framework` IS TRUE
    `his pay is computed by the agreements of a scale the Histadrut represents, for 2001` IS FALSE
    `months employed in 1999–2000, for the 2001 framework` IS 24
    `employed on 1.1.01 or later, for the 2001 framework` IS TRUE

-- Coverage: the nurse is in it, a State teacher is not — by the agreement
-- and by the law.
#ASSERT `owed the 2001 framework grant` `a nurse of the State in 2001`
#ASSERT `owed the 2001 framework supplement` `a nurse of the State in 2001`
#ASSERT NOT `owed the 2001 framework grant` `a teacher of the State in 2001`
#ASSERT NOT `owed the 2001 framework supplement` `a teacher of the State in 2001`
#ASSERT NOT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a general collective agreement` (`the 2001 framework employee, as the law asks` `a teacher of the State in 2001`)
#ASSERT NOT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a special collective agreement` (`the 2001 framework employee, as the law asks` `a teacher of the State in 2001`)
#ASSERT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a special collective agreement` (`the 2001 framework employee, as the law asks` `a nurse of the State in 2001`)

-- §2: the whole grant for the two years in full; half for half a position;
-- 625 for a year in full; a pensioner at 70% for 12 months, 437.5. It is
-- paid with February's or March's salary of 2001, not April's.
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework grant owed` 24 1 EQUALS 1250
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework grant owed` 24 0.5 EQUALS 625
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework grant owed` 12 1 EQUALS 625
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework grant a pensioner is owed` (70%) 12 EQUALS 437.5
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework grant may be paid with the salary of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2001)
#ASSERT NOT `the 2001 framework grant may be paid with the salary of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2001)
#ASSERT NOT `the 2001 framework grant counts for` `the hour value, for the 2001 framework`
#ASSERT `the employer owes the 2001 framework grant to one who left` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the employer owes the 2001 framework grant to one who left` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the employer owes the 2001 framework grant to one who left` TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- §3: 3.6% from 1.1.01, nothing before; on a base of 10,000, 360.
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework supplement rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework supplement` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001) 10000 EQUALS 360
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework supplement is first paid with the salary of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2001)

`the seniority supplement, for 2001` MEANS `2001 framework pay component` WITH
    `the 2001 component's kind` IS `the combined salary, the seniority supplement or a cost-of-living increment, for 2001`
    `the 2001 component is paid monthly, weekly or daily` IS TRUE
    `the 2001 component is updated by the cost-of-living agreements` IS TRUE
    `the 2001 component is counted for the hour value` IS TRUE
`a shekel supplement outside the hour value, for 2001` MEANS `2001 framework pay component` WITH
    `the 2001 component's kind` IS `another supplement in shekels or in percent, for 2001`
    `the 2001 component is paid monthly, weekly or daily` IS TRUE
    `the 2001 component is updated by the cost-of-living agreements` IS TRUE
    `the 2001 component is counted for the hour value` IS FALSE
`a supplement with a mechanism of its own, for 2001` MEANS `2001 framework pay component` WITH
    `the 2001 component's kind` IS `another supplement in shekels or in percent, for 2001`
    `the 2001 component is paid monthly, weekly or daily` IS TRUE
    `the 2001 component is updated by the cost-of-living agreements` IS FALSE
    `the 2001 component is counted for the hour value` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `in the base of the 2001 framework supplement` `the seniority supplement, for 2001`
#ASSERT NOT `in the base of the 2001 framework supplement` `a shekel supplement outside the hour value, for 2001`
#ASSERT `§4 of 2001 raises the component` `a shekel supplement outside the hour value, for 2001`
#ASSERT `the component as §4 of 2001 raises it` `a shekel supplement outside the hour value, for 2001` 100 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001) EQUALS 103.6
#ASSERT `the component as §4 of 2001 raises it` `a supplement with a mechanism of its own, for 2001` 100 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2001) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT NOT `the 2001 framework supplement counts for` `the completion to the minimum wage, for the 2001 framework` TRUE
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework supplement counts for` `the completion to the minimum wage, for the 2001 framework` FALSE
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework supplement counts for` `pensions, for the 2001 framework` TRUE

-- §5: an administrative employee in a grade of the span; a nurse rising
-- past grade 12 from 5,000 to 4,900 keeps 100 as a personal supplement,
-- offset by a rise of 60 to 40 once the completion stops, and kept whole
-- while it is paid.
#ASSERT `in a grade 5.2 lists` "מינהלי" TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `in a grade 5.2 lists` "עובדי הוראה" TRUE
#ASSERT count `the scales and grade spans of 5.2` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework personal supplement` 5000 4900 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework personal supplement` 5000 5100 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework personal supplement after an increase` 100 60 FALSE EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework personal supplement after an increase` 100 60 TRUE EQUALS 100

-- §§6, 9: no other negotiation and industrial peace from the signing to
-- 31.7.01, and not on 1.8.01; §10: a dispute on the supplement declared
-- before the signing is void, one on the pensions' mechanism is not.
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework bars other pay negotiations on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 7 2001)
#ASSERT NOT `the 2001 framework bars other pay negotiations on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2001)
#ASSERT `the 2001 framework's industrial peace holds on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2001)
#ASSERT `a labour dispute is void under the 2001 framework` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2000) `the grant or the supplement, of 2001`
#ASSERT NOT `a labour dispute is void under the 2001 framework` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2000) `the pensions' update mechanism, of 2001`

-- §13: no next agreement — two years; one signed in 2002 — its day.
#ASSERT `the arbitration institution is extended to` NOTHING EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2003
#ASSERT `the arbitration institution is extended to` (JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2002)) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2002
#ASSERT `the arbitration institution is extended to` (JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2004)) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2003

-- The erosion letter and the bill: a 1998 retiree of the administrative
-- scale has 3.2% of a pension of 5,000 from January 2001, 160; a 2000
-- retiree, and a retired policeman, nothing. A claim of a 1998 retiree for
-- 1999 is exhausted, one for 2000 is not. The letter's table and the
